WEBVTT

00:00:27.757 --> 00:00:31.054
Now, we normally share them
in the form of TED Talks,

00:00:31.078 --> 00:00:34.112
which are recorded on a stage,

00:00:34.136 --> 00:00:36.899
12, 15, 18 minutes at a time.

00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:39.020
But here's the thing about ideas:

00:00:39.044 --> 00:00:41.631
they don't just land perfectly formed.

00:00:41.655 --> 00:00:43.500
They want to be critiqued,

00:00:43.524 --> 00:00:45.573
played with, iterated on,

00:00:45.597 --> 00:00:48.896
and sometimes that takes
longer than 18 minutes.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.093
(Music)

00:00:50.117 --> 00:00:53.397
So in this series, I'll be having
hour-long conversations

00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:56.012
with some of the most
compelling TED speakers

00:00:56.036 --> 00:00:59.000
to dive deeper, learn more.

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:03.870
And there is no better medium
to do that dance than podcasting.